{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והזנו את בניך אחרי א", :translit "v'hezinu et banecha acharei a", :gloss "and they cause your children to go astray after [their gods]"} {:he "להיהן", :translit "lahen", :gloss "to them"} {:he "אלהי מסכה", :translit "elohei masseichah", :gloss "gods of molten image"} {:he "ותזנו בם", :translit "vatiznu bam", :gloss "and you committed harlotry with them"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (סמיכות) of להיהן to אלהי מסכה: the root זנו / תזנו connotes both spiritual straying (idolatry) and literal sexual harlotry, applied here to phallic idolatrous forms."}], :frame {:text "The root ז-נ-ה carries the double meaning of idolatry and sexual immorality. Leviticus 20:5 speaks of going astray (לזנה) after Molech as harlotry, and the Ibn Ezra on Numbers 25:1 interprets the Israelites' whoring (ויזן) at Peor as idolatrous straying. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the juxtaposition of 'their gods' with 'molten gods' as encoding literal sexual licentiousness in pagan worship, linking back to the warning in Exodus 34:15–16.", :sources ["Leviticus 20:5" "Ibn Ezra on Numbers 25:1" "Exodus 34:15"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (סמיכות) of להיהן to אלהי מסכה: the root זנו / תזנו connotes both spiritual straying (idolatry) and literal sexual harlotry, applied here to phallic idolatrous forms.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:20:58.125033062Z", :model "glm-5.2"}